{"about_the_game":"The soundtrack to the Crossing The Sands DRPG contains a collection of instrumental songs inspired by Arabic and Mediterranean scales and instruments. Composed and produced by Bloodless Mushroom, these tunes are meant to evoke a bit of the mid-1990's feel, an era when game soundtracks contained MIDI meant to be played through hardware synthesizers such as the Roland SC-88.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEach area of the game has its own feel and style, with some being tranquil, others mysterious, and others agitated to a state of near-panic. Listen now to experience the full range of ambience.","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/2873970?t=1767453408","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/2873970?t=1767453408","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2873970/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1767453408","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2873970/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1767453408","content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"detailed_description":"The soundtrack to the Crossing The Sands DRPG contains a collection of instrumental songs inspired by Arabic and Mediterranean scales and instruments. Composed and produced by Bloodless Mushroom, these tunes are meant to evoke a bit of the mid-1990's feel, an era when game soundtracks contained MIDI meant to be played through hardware synthesizers such as the Roland SC-88.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEach area of the game has its own feel and style, with some being tranquil, others mysterious, and others agitated to a state of near-panic. Listen now to experience the full range of ambience.","developers":["Dragon Dropper"],"fullgame":{"appid":"2505100","name":"Crossing The Sands"},"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2873970/header.jpg?t=1767453408","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":[],"mac_requirements":[